From d0bfb9bdebf1daf91d3d63fffa525cb9a48826d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MarsTechHAN <hansh-sz@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:38:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] [CuTe, SM80] Enable SM8x backward; block-sparse +
 mask_mod backward

- interface: _flash_attn_bwd accepted only 9.x-12.x; add an arch 8.x config
  (SM120 tiling: 64x64 tiles, 4 warps, 1 stage for hdim>64, fits the ~100 KB
  smem of sm86/sm89) and route it to FlashAttentionBackwardSm80.
- FlashAttentionBackwardSm80: add mask_mod (+ aux tensors, fastdiv wrapping
  on boundary tiles) and a block-sparse mainloop over the Q-direction lists
  (block_sparse_tensors_bwd): partial list (mask_mod) then full list, each
  sparse Q block = q_subtile_factor m tiles, sparse KV block = n_block //
  kv_subtile_factor. Q/LSE and dO/dPsum of the next visited m tile are
  prefetched under the dK/dQ GEMMs as in the dense loop; m tiles past
  seqlen_q are skipped; KV tiles with no Q blocks write dK = dV = 0.
  Previously blocksparse_tensors was accepted and ignored here as well.
- compile key for the 8.x/9.x/12.x backward now includes kv_subtile_factor.
- FlashAttnFunc: on SM8x, raise if the forward was block-sparse but no
  block_sparse_tensors_bwd was given (the backward would otherwise silently
  differentiate dense attention).
- block_sparsity: add block_sparse_tensors_fwd_to_bwd() to transpose forward
  KV-direction lists into backward Q-direction lists.
